#############..........##..~~......#bcFL#..~~..^...#sH#......^^..##..T.......#itRS#..........#############READ ME -- this file is a game level stored as a phext. The level lives at addresses 1.1.1/1.1.1/DOWN.LAYER.ACROSS. DOWN is the row (1 = top), LAYER is the section (1 = ground, 2 = things, 3 = what happened -- a level may have more layers), ACROSS is the column. Every scroll at those addresses holds exactly one character: one square of that layer. No scroll means the square is empty. This scroll, at 9.9.9, is reserved for these instructions -- it is never a square, and tools that know the format keep it when they save. To read the level: explode the phext and take its scrolls by coordinate. To change it: set a scroll to a different character, or remove the scroll to empty the square, then implode. Canonical phext libraries: libphext (Rust, on crates.io), phext (Python, on PyPI), libphext (Node and browser, on npm). A level editor, and a kit of tiny reader/writers for Python, Rust, Node, browser JS and C: https://edit.phext.io/ascii-map.html